WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.606 --> 00:00:19.319
The ancient fortress stood on a craggy, windswept ridge on the western slope of Mount Mystery.

2
00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:25.705
Miles of dense, shadowy forest guarded by fearsome creatures separated it from the rest of Magica.

3
00:00:26.406 --> 00:00:28.788
Most people had forgotten the fortress was even there.

4
00:00:29.516 --> 00:00:34.458
But to those who remembered, it was a reminder of the Old Times, when Magica was not the

5
00:00:34.478 --> 00:00:35.759
peaceful place it was now.

6
00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:43.303
A gaunt man with glittering amber eyes stood at a high window staring down at the forest.

7
00:00:44.303 --> 00:00:47.525
He heard a grunt and turned to see that a troll had entered.

8
00:00:47.545 --> 00:00:49.246
"What is it?"

9
00:00:49.766 --> 00:00:50.526
the man demanded.

10
00:00:52.527 --> 00:00:53.768
The troll grunted again.

11
00:00:54.504 --> 00:01:00.347
A puff of magic energy rose above him, showing a rough image of ugly troll teeth tearing into

12
00:01:00.407 --> 00:01:01.968
food. Hungry.

13
00:01:02.328 --> 00:01:03.629
The trolls were hungry.

14
00:01:03.649 --> 00:01:07.691
"You'll have to wait a little longer," the man said.

15
00:01:07.711 --> 00:01:10.993
"But soon you'll have all the food you want."

16
00:01:12.134 --> 00:01:14.655
He stepped over to the contraption in the center of the room.

17
00:01:15.416 --> 00:01:17.137
He'd finished building it moments ago.

18
00:01:17.857 --> 00:01:24.845
It was a mishmash of many things: dragon bones and scales, leather-bound books, stones gathered from the Cave

19
00:01:24.885 --> 00:01:26.167
of the Unknown, and more.

20
00:01:26.947 --> 00:01:31.271
At the very top of the pile was an ancient human skull bleached white by time.

21
00:01:32.031 --> 00:01:35.734
The man rubbed his hands together and placed them over the skull's eye sockets.

22
00:01:36.855 --> 00:01:42.880
The machine shuddered to life and belched out an image: a map of all of Magica.

23
00:01:43.501 --> 00:01:45.502
Tiny red dots glowed here and there.

24
00:01:45.963 --> 00:01:46.683
Hundreds of them!

25
00:01:47.364 --> 00:01:48.204
The man smiled.

26
00:01:48.865 --> 00:01:52.388
The Secret Eye worked, just as the ancient writings had predicted.

27
00:01:53.148 --> 00:01:54.648
This would make things much easier.

28
00:01:57.829 --> 00:02:00.510
It was time to go and take what was rightfully his.

29
00:02:02.331 --> 00:02:05.331
"Zann, you're next.

30
00:02:05.831 --> 00:02:07.772
Zann. Zann!

31
00:02:08.612 --> 00:02:11.793
ZANN!" Zann blinked and looked at the teacher.

32
00:02:11.813 --> 00:02:14.734
"Sorry, Professor Liblow," he said.

33
00:02:14.754 --> 00:02:16.054
"Could you repeat that?"

34
00:02:16.734 --> 00:02:18.535
Several of Zann's classmates laughed.

35
00:02:18.555 --> 00:02:24.193
"It's your turn to perform today's exercise," Professor Liblow said patiently.

36
00:02:24.213 --> 00:02:28.435
"Please move your assigned objects according to my instructions."

37
00:02:29.536 --> 00:02:30.616
"Oh. Okay."

38
00:02:31.037 --> 00:02:31.757
Zann stood up.

39
00:02:32.778 --> 00:02:33.818
Everyone was watching him.

40
00:02:34.559 --> 00:02:39.181
He had no idea what instructions the teacher had given or what his assigned objects were.

41
00:02:39.941 --> 00:02:41.362
He'd been too busy daydreaming.

42
00:02:42.063 --> 00:02:43.864
He looked at the table at the front of the room.

43
00:02:44.624 --> 00:02:49.267
All sorts of things were sitting there—fruit, rocks, shoes, and more.

44
00:02:49.967 --> 00:02:51.668
Which items was he supposed to move?

45
00:02:52.288 --> 00:02:56.291
"Books," a voice hissed behind him, too softly for the teacher to hear.

46
00:02:56.311 --> 00:02:59.133
"You're supposed to stack them by size."

47
00:03:00.113 --> 00:03:02.495
It was Perda, his next-door neighbor and friend.

48
00:03:03.195 --> 00:03:04.416
He shot her a grateful look.

49
00:03:05.117 --> 00:03:06.638
Then he glanced at the books.

50
00:03:07.778 --> 00:03:09.159
Transporting stuff was easy.

51
00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:13.442
But it wasn't easy to do it with the control and precision that the teacher wanted.

52
00:03:14.163 --> 00:03:16.396
Especially for someone like Zann.

53
00:03:16.416 --> 00:03:22.299
He was good at bigger magic, like zapping himself to a new place or creating clothing or food

54
00:03:22.379 --> 00:03:22.940
out of nothing.

55
00:03:24.241 --> 00:03:27.322
This smaller, more detailed type of magic was not easy.

56
00:03:28.023 --> 00:03:31.925
It required a quiet mind, and Zann's mind was rarely quiet.

57
00:03:32.605 --> 00:03:34.646
He rubbed his thumb against his other fingers.

58
00:03:35.307 --> 00:03:38.449
There was a crackling sound as sparks began to jump from his hand.

59
00:03:39.149 --> 00:03:44.052
Zann pointed at the largest book, and everything on the table flew into the air and exploded.

60
00:03:45.676 --> 00:03:48.659
The other students giggled, and Zann smiled sheepishly.

61
00:03:49.319 --> 00:03:50.420
"Oops," he said.

62
00:03:50.440 --> 00:03:51.941
"Sorry about that."

63
00:03:52.642 --> 00:03:54.643
Professor Liblow rubbed his hands together.

64
00:03:54.663 --> 00:03:56.905
"Restore!" he said.

65
00:03:56.925 --> 00:03:58.166
The items reappeared.

66
00:03:58.186 --> 00:04:01.009
"Try again, please, Zann.

67
00:04:01.689 --> 00:04:03.511
And try to focus this time.

68
00:04:04.371 --> 00:04:09.696
We don't want you accidentally transporting the entire school to the peak of Mount Mystery."

69
00:04:10.737 --> 00:04:13.099
That made everyone laugh, including Zann.

70
00:04:13.719 --> 00:04:14.540
Then he tried again.

71
00:04:14.932 --> 00:04:17.153
This time he did his best to focus.

72
00:04:17.173 --> 00:04:19.733
"Come to me," he murmured.

73
00:04:20.454 --> 00:04:22.394
Now only the largest book rose.

74
00:04:23.094 --> 00:04:25.735
It flew through the air and landed gently on his desk.

75
00:04:26.555 --> 00:04:28.876
One by one, he brought the other books to him.

76
00:04:29.676 --> 00:04:35.137
Finally a slim volume titled Dragon Taming Tips landed neatly atop the pile.

77
00:04:36.138 --> 00:04:37.198
Most of the class clapped.

78
00:04:37.558 --> 00:04:38.718
Zann gave a playful bow.

79
00:04:38.738 --> 00:04:41.859
"Pretty slow," a boy said loudly.

80
00:04:41.879 --> 00:04:44.640
"And you had to use a focusing phrase.

81
00:04:45.460 --> 00:04:48.601
I thought Reds were supposed to be better at magic than the rest of us."

82
00:04:49.461 --> 00:04:52.022
"Enough, Jev," the teacher said sternly.

83
00:04:52.042 --> 00:04:55.603
"If you think you can do better, you may go next."

84
00:04:56.443 --> 00:04:57.324
Zann sat down.

85
00:04:57.344 --> 00:05:00.724
"Thanks for saving me," he whispered to his friend.

86
00:05:01.745 --> 00:05:02.805
Perda leaned forward.

87
00:05:02.825 --> 00:05:04.185
"No problem.

88
00:05:04.446 --> 00:05:06.966
But you really should pay attention," she whispered.

89
00:05:06.986 --> 00:05:10.767
"Even Reds can't just fake their way through every class they don't like."

90
00:05:11.588 --> 00:05:12.468
Zann didn't answer.

91
00:05:13.216 --> 00:05:15.937
Physical Objects was one of his least favorite classes.

92
00:05:16.617 --> 00:05:20.098
It was boring—even more boring than Food and Drink Creation.

93
00:05:20.798 --> 00:05:23.579
When would he ever need to move things around like that, anyway?

94
00:05:24.459 --> 00:05:27.700
He wasn't planning on becoming a physical builder or anything of the sort.

95
00:05:28.040 --> 00:05:28.500
No way.

96
00:05:29.181 --> 00:05:31.401
He was going to be an explorer like his parents.

97
00:05:32.101 --> 00:05:35.922
That's why he spent most of his time in school daydreaming about exciting adventures.

98
00:05:35.942 --> 00:05:37.583
"I'm finished!"

99
00:05:37.963 --> 00:05:41.084
Jev announced as he lined up one last shoe on his desk.

100
00:05:41.824 --> 00:05:43.245
He shot Zann a smug look.

101
00:05:43.265 --> 00:05:45.306
"Much faster than the Red."

102
00:05:46.027 --> 00:05:46.808
Zann frowned.

103
00:05:47.488 --> 00:05:49.329
Jev always had to make him look bad.

104
00:05:50.230 --> 00:05:53.292
Just then a pretty girl named Gliss pointed to the door.

105
00:05:53.992 --> 00:05:56.914
Gliss was the only other Red in the class besides Zann.

106
00:05:56.934 --> 00:05:58.616
"An echo crow!"

107
00:05:58.996 --> 00:05:59.436
she cried.

108
00:06:00.137 --> 00:06:02.838
A large, purple-feathered crow flapped into the room.

109
00:06:06.741 --> 00:06:08.182
Message!" it squawked.

110
00:06:08.202 --> 00:06:10.644
"Urgent message from the king and queen!"

111
00:06:11.692 --> 00:06:14.753
Several kids gasped, and Zann sat up straight in his chair.

112
00:06:15.473 --> 00:06:21.795
He couldn't remember anyone from Magica's capital, First City, sending a message to boring old Swamp Bottom before.

113
00:06:22.496 --> 00:06:23.916
Especially not the king and queen!

114
00:06:23.936 --> 00:06:26.977
"Hush," Professor Liblow told the class.

115
00:06:27.657 --> 00:06:28.878
Then he nodded to the crow.

116
00:06:28.898 --> 00:06:29.978
"Go on, please."

117
00:06:30.718 --> 00:06:31.919
"Urgent! Danger!"

118
00:06:32.259 --> 00:06:33.039
the crow squawked.

119
00:06:33.059 --> 00:06:34.759
"Danger for all
